{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/200483-totem-peach-guzenuthfara-nirkaya-the-sun-gilded-peacock","id":200483,"title":"[Totem/PEACH] Guzenuthfara-Nirkaya - The Sun-Gilded Peacock","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-17T16:08:51-07:00","id":200483,"title":"[Totem/PEACH] Guzenuthfara-Nirkaya - The Sun-Gilded Peacock","content":"<b><i>Edit: </i></b><i>Post-GMC stats have now been made available.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b><i>Guzenuthfara-Nirkaya:</i> <br /> The Sun-Gilded Peacock</b></div> <br /> The Sun-Gilded Peacock is a most regal spirit, and is known by many names \u2014 The Gilded Lord, The Master of Wolves and Birds, The King-In-Gold-and-Silver, The Splendidly-Winged, The Immortal Peacock, The Light-Bearing Emperor, The Undying Raj. He appears as a horse-sized peacock, shimmering with power and glowing like a second sun. Decked in feathers of gold, he struts forward with his head held high, flashing his dazzling eyespots that can either hypnotize or blind others. He is resilient and undying, embodying the splendour and pomp of power, fame and royalty, and the lingering legacies of the elite who have never been forgotten. He is the overpowering might of Genghis Khan and Alexander; the ruthlessness and decadence of old European courts; the adoration and celebration of El Cid and Joan of Arc. He never follows, never admits to being weaker or lesser, and tolerates not disrespect or doubt. He is the totem of those who rule above all, unconcerned if it is through might, magic or manipulation \u2014 morality is not something he has dominion over, nor is it something he's concerned with.<br /> <br /> It's no surprise Nirkaya is demanding. In exchange for the things he grants his followers, he only asks in return to be worshipped and adored. His followers become his princes and puppet-kings, sharing a fraction of their true master's power in order to further themselves in the world. If displeased, tantrums and full-blown, violent backlashes are not above Nirkaya \u2014 and he has the strength and abilities to prove it. After all, spirits in Nirkaya's position don't get where they are by hiding and keeping their head down; he is a very bold, very forward beast, and has devoured a few Uratha in the past when deemed necessary.<br /> <br /> Storm Lords and Ivory Claws most often take Sun-Gilded as a totem. Nirkaya prefers the latter over the former \u2014 the Pure are not above throwing themselves at the feet of spirits, and Skolis-Ur always has the last say with the Iminir \u2014 but some Lord-packs have impressed him enough. To a lesser extent, the Blood Talons honour him for how he refuses to accept insult, and how little he thinks of giving up or surrendering. Iron Masters in high or wealthy positions \u2014 bankers, CEOs, movie directors \u2014 will also seek him out to reaffirm their position, though most are uneasy at Nirkaya's demands; he has asked before for wolves to sacrifice territory for him. Hunters In Darkness are also uneasy with such requests, and his one-sided demands are often hell for Bone Shadows to follow up on. Fire-Touched find him outright blasphemous, and Predator Kings are split on him \u2014 on the one hand, his ruthlessness and strength resonates in many hearts. On the other hand, his pettiness, combined with the fact he takes the form of a prey animal, make many want to eat him.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves are an interesting case with Nirkaya. He does not voice this fact to many, but in the past, he has gathered large numbers of Thihirtha Numea under his wing. Their lack of allegiance to any of the Firstborn makes them ideal for total devotion to him, and he has even fancied gathering enough to form a new tribe or lodge. The latter has nearly come to pass several times, but it's an unfortunate fact that Nirkaya's followers burn out quickly with what he asks. At least a few of them made for tasty Essence in a pinch....<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pre-GMC Stats:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Spirit Ban: </b>Guzenuthfara-Nirkaya can never admit guilt or fault to anything, and never can he admit if he's lost any game, conflict, and the like. He is always perfect and always right; if he is somehow coerced into saying or communicating otherwise, he loses all his numina for an entire scene, and all his attributes drop to 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem Ban:</b> Followers of Guzenuthfara-Nirkaya must always answer their totem's demands. Whether or not they are compromised by such demands is secondary; Guzenuthfara-Nirkaya is their Lord and King, and they <i>will</i> answer to him. Like the Sun-Gilded Peacock, they must also never admit to guilt or fault, and never admit to having lost something. This totem also expects regular offerings and entertainment, whether it be food (physical or in the form of spirits), music and dance, human sacrifice, etc.<br /> <br /> <i>Power:</i> *****-*<br /> <i>Finesse:</i> *****-*<br /> <i>Resistance:</i> *****-***<br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b><br /> <i>Fear: </i>*<br /> <i>Leadership:</i> *<br /> <i>Pride:</i> *<br /> <br /> <b>Total Totem Points: </b>25 (Rank 3 Spirit)<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>16/16<br /> <b>Essence: </b>20/20<br /> <b>Corpus: </b>14/14<br /> <b>Size: </b>6<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>12<br /> <b>Speed: </b>18<br /> <b>Defense: </b>6<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Numina:</b><ul><li>Compulsion (3 points)</li> <li>Consume Offering (3 points)</li> <li>Material Vision (free)</li> <li>Materialize (3 points)</li> <li>Reaching (3 points)</li> </ul><b>Bonuses:</b><ul><li>Pack can choose from either +1 Skill Bonus (pack) to Empathy, Politics or Intimidation - pack has to choose one and remain with it for the rest of the story (3 points)</li> <li>Free specialty in Politics, of the pack's choice and for the rest of the story (2 points)</li> <li>Once per story, a +1 to one Social attribute of the pack's choice, and for the rest of the story (3 points)</li> <li>An extra Willpower dot per story to draw from (2 points)</li> <li>Once per story, the ability to either use the gift Warning Growl or Sense Guilt; the pack must pick one or the other and use it for the rest of the story (3 points)</li> </ul><i><b>Further Options:</b></i> The Lone Wolf Chronicle (<i>Forsaken Chronicler\u2019s Guide</i>)<br /> <br /> In chronicles featuring Lone Wolves (see pg. 23 and onwards in the <i>Forsaken Chronicler\u2019s Guide</i>), Guzenuthfara-Nirkaya may or may accept a Lone Wolf under his patronage. He admires the ambition of those who would have him all for themselves, but at the same time, he is much harder on them than he is a pack. Whereas a pack has numbers and resources to devote to him, the Lone Wolf is a single creature, and walking alone doesn\u2019t exactly bring you many followers. Still, those who prove their mettle may find a powerful ally in this spirit. It\u2019s up to the ST on whether Nirkaya is an option or not.<br /> <br /> In addition to the bonuses provided above, Lone Wolves can pick from one of three blessings provided on pages 25-26 of the <i>Chronicler\u2019s Guide</i>: <b>Discerning, Gravitas</b> or <b>Spiritual</b>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Post-GMC Stats:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Totem and Lone Wolf options aren't listed here because there isn't a system in place yet for converting them over. Talk with your ST on post-GMC totems; I know everyone has their own options for stop-gaps while we wait for the Idigam Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Ban: </b>Guzenuthfara-Nirkaya can never admit guilt or fault to anything, and never can he admit if he's lost any game, conflict, and the like. He is always perfect and always right; if he is somehow coerced into saying or communicating otherwise, he loses all his numina for an entire scene, and all his attributes drop to 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Bane: </b>Guzenuthfara-Nirkaya, oddly enough, is repelled by the touch of &quot;sky iron&quot;, or iron obtained from meteorites. In folklore, iron is often the bane of many creatures, and Nirkaya is no exception; it is said that this weakness is a curse upon him. Apparently, there was a powerful Incarna that Nirkaya mouthed off to, and the Incarna saw fit to hurl a hex-imbued space rock at Nirkaya's face....<br /> <br /> <i>Power:</i> *****-*<br /> <i>Finesse:</i> *****-*<br /> <i>Resistance:</i> *****-***<br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b><br /> <i>Fear: </i>*<br /> <i>Leadership:</i> *<br /> <i>Pride:</i> *<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus: </b>14/14<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>12<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestations:</b><ul><li>Discorporate</li> <li>Materialize</li> <li>Reaching</li> <li>Twilight Form</li> </ul><b>Numina:</b><ul><li>Aggressive Meme</li> <li>Awe</li> <li><i>Consume Offering </i>- Like the Essence Thief numina, only replace Essence with offerings such as food, blood, etc.</li> <li>Drain</li> <li>Implant Mission</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-18-2014, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avata